---
import type { ToolEntry } from '../../lib/tools/registry';

interface Props {
  tool: ToolEntry;
}

const { tool } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="tool-seo-section" id="educational-guide" aria-label={`${tool.name} Technical Guide & Reference`}>
  <div class="seo-wrap">
    <header class="seo-header">
      <div class="seo-badge">TECHNICAL REFERENCE & COMPLIANCE GUIDE</div>
      <h2>{tool.name} Explained</h2>
      <p class="seo-intro">
        An in-depth electrical engineering guide to conductor physics, cable sizing formulas, and international wiring regulations (BS 7671 & IEC 60364).
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="seo-grid">
      <article class="seo-article">
        <!-- Section 1: Overview -->
        <section class="seo-block">
          <h3>What is Voltage Drop in Electrical Cables?</h3>
          <p>
            Whenever electric current flows through an electrical cable, energy is dissipated as heat due to the internal resistance of the metallic conductor.
            This resistance causes a reduction in electrical potential along the length of the wire, meaning the voltage delivered to the load is lower than the voltage supplied at the source origin.
          </p>
          <p>
            For example, in a <strong>230 V single-phase circuit</strong> delivering <strong>40 A</strong> over a <strong>50-meter</strong> run of <strong>10 mm² copper cable</strong>,
            the total conductor resistance creates a voltage drop of approximately <strong>6.33 V (2.75%)</strong>.
            The load receives <strong>223.67 V</strong>, safely within BS 7671 permissible limits.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2: Mathematical Equations & Derivations -->
        {tool.equations && tool.equations.length > 0 && (
          <section class="seo-block">
            <h3>The Voltage Drop Formulas & Equations</h3>
            <div class="seo-formulas-grid">
              {tool.equations.map((eq) => (
                <div class="seo-formula-card">
                  <div class="formula-head">
                    <span class="formula-icon">📐</span>
                    <h4>{eq.title}</h4>
                  </div>
                  <code>{eq.formula}</code>
                  <p>{eq.description}</p>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>
        )}

        <!-- Section 3: How-To Step by Step -->
        {tool.steps && tool.steps.length > 0 && (
          <section class="seo-block">
            <h3>How to Calculate Voltage Drop: Step-by-Step</h3>
            <ol class="seo-steps-list">
              {tool.steps.map((s, idx) => (
                <li class="seo-step-item">
                  <div class="step-num">{idx + 1}</div>
                  <div class="step-content">
                    <h4>{s.step}</h4>
                    <p>{s.instruction}</p>
                  </div>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ol>
          </section>
        )}

        <!-- Section 4: BS 7671 Limits Table -->
        <section class="seo-block">
          <h3>BS 7671 & IEC 60364 Permissible Voltage Drop Limits</h3>
          <p>
            Under UK Wiring Regulations (BS 7671:2018+A3:2024 Appendix 4) and international IEC standards, maximum permitted voltage drop from the origin of the public supply installation to any point of utilization is:
          </p>
          <div class="seo-table-wrap">
            <table class="seo-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Installation Type</th>
                  <th>Lighting Circuits (Max %)</th>
                  <th>Other Uses: Sockets, Power, Heating (Max %)</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Public Low-Voltage Supply (Standard)</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="table-tag good">3.0% (6.9 V at 230 V)</span></td>
                  <td><span class="table-tag good">5.0% (11.5 V at 230 V)</span></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>Private Low-Voltage Supply (Solar PV / Generator)</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="table-tag warning">6.0% (13.8 V at 230 V)</span></td>
                  <td><span class="table-tag warning">8.0% (18.4 V at 230 V)</span></td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 5: Mitigation Techniques -->
        <section class="seo-block">
          <h3>How to Reduce Voltage Drop in Long Cable Runs</h3>
          <ul class="seo-checklist">
            <li><strong>Upsize Conductor Cross-Section:</strong> Increasing from 6 mm² to 10 mm² or 16 mm² halves conductor resistance, drastically reducing voltage loss and heat build-up.</li>
            <li><strong>Shorten Cable Routing:</strong> Optimize cable paths through containment and cable trays to eliminate unnecessary run length.</li>
            <li><strong>Switch to Higher Voltages or Three-Phase:</strong> For large industrial loads, distributing load across three phases reduces current per conductor by a factor of 1.732.</li>
            <li><strong>Use High-Conductivity Copper:</strong> Electrolytic tough pitch copper has ~64% lower resistivity than aluminum conductors of the same physical dimensions.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 6: Interactive FAQs Accordion -->
        {tool.faqs && tool.faqs.length > 0 && (
          <section class="seo-block" id="faq-section">
            <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
            <div class="seo-faq-accordion">
              {tool.faqs.map((faq) => (
                <details class="faq-item">
                  <summary class="faq-question">
                    <span>{faq.question}</span>
                    <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="faq-answer">
                    <p>{faq.answer}</p>
                  </div>
                </details>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>
        )}
      </article>

      <!-- Sidebar Simulator CTA & Related Guides -->
      <aside class="seo-sidebar">
        <div class="simulator-cta-card">
          <div class="sim-badge">INTERACTIVE LAB</div>
          <h3 class="sim-title">Want to test this circuit in ElectraSim?</h3>
          <p class="sim-desc">
            Take your calculated voltage, cable, and load values into the ElectraSim Wiring Simulator.
            Add circuit breakers, switches, lights, and test faults interactively in real time.
          </p>
          <a href="/app/" class="btn-launch-sim">
            <span>Build Circuit in ElectraSim</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        {tool.relatedGuides && tool.relatedGuides.length > 0 && (
          <div class="related-tools-card">
            <h4 class="rel-title">Related Technical Guides</h4>
            <ul class="rel-list">
              {tool.relatedGuides.map((guide) => (
                <li class="rel-item">
                  <a href={guide.url} class="rel-link">
                    <span class="rel-item-title">{guide.title}</span>
                    <span class="rel-item-desc">{guide.description}</span>
                  </a>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        )}
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .tool-seo-section {
    background: var(--bg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 5rem 0 6rem;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 10;
  }
  .seo-wrap {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .seo-header {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto 4rem;
  }
  .seo-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--blue-l);
    color: var(--blue);
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-bright);
  }
  .seo-header h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .seo-intro {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-mid);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .seo-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px;
    gap: 3.5rem;
  }
  .seo-article {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }
  .seo-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .seo-block h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.45rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .seo-block p {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: var(--body-copy, var(--text-mid));
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .seo-formulas-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .seo-formula-card {
    padding: 1.25rem 1.35rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
  }
  .formula-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }
  .formula-head h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .seo-formula-card code {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--blue);
    background: var(--bg-2);
    padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 0.45rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }
  .seo-formula-card p {
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .seo-steps-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .seo-step-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .step-num {
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--blue);
    color: #ffffff;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    shrink: 0;
  }
  .step-content h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
  }
  .step-content p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .seo-table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .seo-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .seo-table th {
    background: var(--bg-3);
    padding: 0.95rem 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .seo-table td {
    padding: 0.95rem 1.15rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-mid);
  }
  .seo-table tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .table-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 0.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .table-tag.good {
    background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.12);
    color: #10b981;
  }
  .table-tag.warning {
    background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12);
    color: #f59e0b;
  }
  .seo-checklist {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }
  .seo-checklist li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.85rem;
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    color: var(--body-copy, var(--text-mid));
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .seo-checklist li::before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    color: #10b981;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  /* FAQ Accordion */
  .seo-faq-accordion {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .faq-item {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg-card);
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .faq-item[open] {
    border-color: var(--border-bright);
  }
  .faq-question {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    user-select: none;
  }
  .faq-question::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .faq-chevron {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }
  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 1.25rem 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .faq-answer p {
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    color: var(--text-mid);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }

  /* Sidebar */
  .seo-sidebar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .simulator-cta-card {
    padding: 2.25rem 1.75rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, #1e3a8a 0%, #2563eb 100%);
    color: #ffffff;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 36px -6px rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.35);
  }
  .sim-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-bottom: 1.15rem;
  }
  .sim-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.38rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .sim-desc {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: #bfdbfe;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.65rem;
  }
  .btn-launch-sim {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0.95rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 0.65rem;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #1e3a8a;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    text-decoration: none;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, background 0.15s ease;
  }
  .btn-launch-sim:hover {
    background: #eff6ff;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .related-tools-card {
    padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .rel-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1.15rem;
  }
  .rel-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .rel-link {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .rel-item-title {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.4;
    transition: color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .rel-item-desc {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .rel-link:hover .rel-item-title {
    color: var(--blue);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .seo-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
